            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-connective-role",
        "moduleId": "logic-as-language",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "把 connective 看成句子连接词",
        "markdown": "把 statement 当作句子、connective 当作连接词，本点先确认哪些句子是 statement，再看每个 connective 如何由分句真值决定复合句真值，于是“文法”落实为可逐行检查的真值表。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-logic-as-grammar"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tb-statements",
        "moduleId": "statements-and-truth",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "statement 与 truth value",
        "markdown": "能明确判断对错的论述称为 statement，例如 $2>0$；而 $x>0$ 在 $x$ 未指定时不是 statement。statement 的真值只有 T、F 两种。“今天天气很热”因标准不明不是 statement；“天空打雷会下雨”有时真有时假也不是，而“天空打雷一定会下雨”才是真值为 F 的 statement。数学常省略“一定”，故有时对有时错的论述按假处理。若干 statements 可由 connectives 组合成新 statement。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d79ad0eadaa0dc69704ecc53",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000002"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Basic Logic",
                "Connectives"
              ],
              "lineStart": 7,
              "lineEnd": 42,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "d99be536e7c4cb65e2c4733f273a3f5a3946f5f3019013237d74bc801b82d5bc"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-statement-check",
        "moduleId": "statements-and-truth",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "判断 statement 的两个检查点",
        "markdown": "判断 statement 可问两点：是否有明确对错标准，真值在讨论范围内是否固定。$x>0$ 在 $x$ 未指定时两点都不满足；而“对所有实数 $x$，$x>0$”真值固定为 F，是 statement。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-statements"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tb-and-or",
        "moduleId": "conjunction-and-disjunction",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "合取与析取：and 与 or",
        "markdown": "$P \\land Q$ 是 $P,Q$ 的 conjunction，只有 $P,Q$ 都真才真，否则为假。$P \\lor Q$ 是 disjunction，采用 inclusive or：至少一个为真就真，只有都假才假，所以“$4<5$ or $4>3$”仍为真。日常“可乐或果汁”式二选一是 exclusive or，数学的 or 不排除同真。混合使用时如 $(P \\land Q) \\lor R$ 与 $P \\land (Q \\lor R)$ 结构不同，不能默认等价。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d79ad0eadaa0dc69704ecc53",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000002"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Basic Logic",
                "Connectives"
              ],
              "lineStart": 7,
              "lineEnd": 42,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "d99be536e7c4cb65e2c4733f273a3f5a3946f5f3019013237d74bc801b82d5bc"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-inclusive-or-check",
        "moduleId": "conjunction-and-disjunction",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "comparison",
        "title": "两种 or 的真值差异",
        "markdown": "inclusive or 只在 $P,Q$ 都假时为假；exclusive or 在 $P,Q$ 同真时也为假。判断题目中的“或”属于哪种，先问“两者同时成立时结论还成立吗”。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-and-or"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tb-conditional",
        "moduleId": "conditional",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "if-then 与 conditional",
        "markdown": "$P \\Rightarrow Q$ 是 conditional，读作“if $P$ then $Q$”。$P$ 真 $Q$ 假时为假，$P$ 真 $Q$ 真时为真；$P$ 假时无论 $Q$ 真假都为真，因为条件句只承诺“$P$ 成立时 $Q$ 一定成立”。所以 $P \\Rightarrow Q$ 与 $Q \\Rightarrow P$ 不同：由“if $x>3$ then $x^2>9$”不能推出“if $x^2>9$ then $x>3$”。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d79ad0eadaa0dc69704ecc53",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000002"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Basic Logic",
                "Connectives"
              ],
              "lineStart": 7,
              "lineEnd": 42,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "d99be536e7c4cb65e2c4733f273a3f5a3946f5f3019013237d74bc801b82d5bc"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-implication-boundary",
        "moduleId": "conditional",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "misconception",
        "title": "条件句不是因果也不可逆",
        "markdown": "别把 $P \\Rightarrow Q$ 读成“有因果且可逆”。逻辑 connective 允许 $P,Q$ 毫无关系，如“if $3>2$ then 2 is even”；真值表只规定真值组合，不提供因果，也不允许反向。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-conditional"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-contrapositive-question",
        "moduleId": "conditional",
        "depth": "advanced",
        "kind": "exercise",
        "title": "练习：由 Q 假反推 P",
        "markdown": "练习：已知 $P \\Rightarrow Q$ 为真，发现 $Q$ 为假时能否断言 $P$ 为假？答案：能。真值表中使 $P \\Rightarrow Q$ 为假的唯一情形是 $P$ 真 $Q$ 假；已知 $Q$ 假而条件句仍真，故 $P$ 只能为假。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-conditional"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tb-biconditional",
        "moduleId": "biconditional",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "if and only if 与 biconditional",
        "markdown": "把 $(P \\Rightarrow Q) \\land (Q \\Rightarrow P)$ 记为 $P \\Leftrightarrow Q$，读作“$P$ if and only if $Q$”，即“$P$ 当且仅当 $Q$”，称为 biconditional。它为真要求 $P,Q$ 同真或同假，一真一假时为假。教材由此解释：要让双条件在 $P,Q$ 同假时为真，必须把 $P$ 假时的 $P \\Rightarrow Q$ 定义为真。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d79ad0eadaa0dc69704ecc53",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000002"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Basic Logic",
                "Connectives"
              ],
              "lineStart": 7,
              "lineEnd": 42,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "d99be536e7c4cb65e2c4733f273a3f5a3946f5f3019013237d74bc801b82d5bc"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-biconditional-check",
        "moduleId": "biconditional",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "note",
        "title": "双条件的快捷判断",
        "markdown": "判断 $P \\Leftrightarrow Q$：逐行比较 $P,Q$ 真值，相同为 T、不同为 F；也可检查两个方向的条件句是否同时成立。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-biconditional"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tb-truth-tables",
        "moduleId": "truth-tables-and-equivalence",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "mechanism",
        "title": "真值表与复合 statement 的求值",
        "markdown": "truth table 列出 $P,Q$ 的每种真值组合并写出复合结果。$(P \\land Q) \\land R$ 先算 $P \\land Q$ 再与 $R$ 联结，$P \\land (Q \\land R)$ 先算 $Q \\land R$；逐行比较真值表可知二者 logically equivalent，故可写成 $P \\land Q \\land R$。$\\land$、$\\lor$ 各自满足交换律与结合律，混合时则要靠分配关系与括号。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d79ad0eadaa0dc69704ecc53",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000002"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Basic Logic",
                "Connectives"
              ],
              "lineStart": 7,
              "lineEnd": 42,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "d99be536e7c4cb65e2c4733f273a3f5a3946f5f3019013237d74bc801b82d5bc"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-truth-table-practice",
        "moduleId": "truth-tables-and-equivalence",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "procedure",
        "title": "列真值表的步骤",
        "markdown": "1）有 $n$ 个原子 statement 就列 $2^n$ 行；2）从最内层子式按括号计算；3）把每行结果填入最外层 connective 的列；4）比较两个 statement forms 的最终列，全部相同才 logically equivalent。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-truth-tables"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tb-logical-equivalence",
        "moduleId": "truth-tables-and-equivalence",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "statement form 与 logical equivalence",
        "markdown": "$P,Q$ 作为可变占位符时，由 connectives 联结的式子称为 statement form。两个 statement forms 若在所有真值指派下真值表完全相同，就称 logically equivalent，记作 $(P \\land Q) \\sim (Q \\land P)$。等价性描述的是 statement forms 的关系，而非已确定的 statements。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d79ad0eadaa0dc69704ecc53",
